      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the progressive side, students could argue that systemic barriers require active intervention, such as targeted resource allocation, to level the playing field. The revolutionary perspective might focus on fundamental structural changes to dismantle existing power imbalances entirely. Conversely, the regressive/stubborn side could argue that everyone should be treated identically under current rules, believing that individual effort is the only true factor in success. Finally, the \"stubborn\" stance could insist that the current system is already fair, regardless of outcomes.",
      "source": "target",
